    },
    {
      "id": "text-0123",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1344,
      "y": 898,
      "width": 419.04,
      "height": 30.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0121"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 926767605,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 251539460,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The idea: long multiplication in binary",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The idea: long multiplication in binary",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "text-0124",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1344,
      "y": 938.0,
      "width": 490.5,
      "height": 180.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0121"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 818140168,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1989179696,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In decimal, 23 × 12 = 23 × 2 + 23 × 10: one shifted copy\nof 23 for each digit of 12. Binary works the same way, but\nevery digit is 0 or 1, so each row is either a shifted copy\nof integer1 (digit 1) or nothing at all (digit 0).\nShifting left by one place multiplies by 2, so the rows are\n6 × 1, 6 × 2, 6 × 4 = 6, 12, 24 (110, 1100, 11000).\n5 = 101 = 4 + 1 picks the rows for 1 and 4:\n6 × 5 = 24 + 6 = 30.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In decimal, 23 × 12 = 23 × 2 + 23 × 10: one shifted copy\nof 23 for each digit of 12. Binary works the same way, but\nevery digit is 0 or 1, so each row is either a shifted copy\nof integer1 (digit 1) or nothing at all (digit 0).\nShifting left by one place multiplies by 2, so the rows are\n6 × 1, 6 × 2, 6 × 4 = 6, 12, 24 (110, 1100, 11000).\n5 = 101 = 4 + 1 picks the rows for 1 and 4:\n6 × 5 = 24 + 6 = 30.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "text-0126",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 435.6,
      "height": 25.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18349992,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 818472949,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The idea as long multiplication: 6 × 5 in binary",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The idea as long multiplication: 6 × 5 in binary",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
